                            <comment id="493041" author="adilger" created="Mon, 13 Apr 2026 21:07:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Keguang, could you please look into this test failure.  The sanity test_908 was added by your patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/56691&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/56691&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17309&quot; title=&quot;set timestamp on llog objects at creation time&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-17309&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17309&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; llog: set timestamp on llog objects at creation time&quot;), see test failure reports at:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?end_date=2026-04-12&amp;amp;source=sub_tests&amp;amp;start_date=2026-04-06&amp;amp;status=FAIL&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=1c94eb71-200e-4e5e-95f5-d5ee0c5ad4b2&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?end_date=2026-04-12&amp;amp;source=sub_tests&amp;amp;start_date=2026-04-06&amp;amp;status=FAIL&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=1c94eb71-200e-4e5e-95f5-d5ee0c5ad4b2&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It looks like it has been failing intermittently during testing, sometimes during branch testing runs, and sometimes during interop teset runs with 2.16.0 MDS because the tests are checking for &quot;&lt;tt&gt;(( MDS1_VERSION &amp;gt;= $(version_code 2.16.0) ))&lt;/tt&gt;&quot;.  In fact, this patch was not landed until commit &lt;tt&gt;v2_16_50-161-ge33d196b93&lt;/tt&gt;, so it wouldn&apos;t have been included into a release until 2.17.0.   Please update the test interop checks to use:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
        (( MDS1_VERSION &amp;gt;= $(version_code v2_16_50-161-ge33d196b93) )) ||
                skip &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;need MDS &amp;gt;= 2.16.50.161 &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; llog timestamps&quot;&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;tt&gt;version_code&lt;/tt&gt; function can handle the &quot;&lt;tt&gt;git describe&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; format and will consider this to be the same version as &quot;&lt;tt&gt;2.16.50.161&lt;/tt&gt;&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493045" author="adilger" created="Mon, 13 Apr 2026 21:33:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It looks like these failures are only happening during the &quot;rolling upgrade&quot; tests, where the filesystem formatted with an old release, then upgraded to a new release.  In this case, the &lt;tt&gt;params&lt;/tt&gt; file was initially written with 2.15 or 2.16 and did not get a timestamp set at creation time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It looks like it is possible to extract the Lustre version used when the &lt;tt&gt;params&lt;/tt&gt; file was written, by adding the following check into the test:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
        local format_ver=($(lctl --device MGS llog_print --raw params | awk &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;/version/ { print $10 }&apos;&lt;/span&gt;))
        (( $(version_code $format_ver) &amp;gt; $(version_code v2_16_50-161-ge33d196b93) )) ||
                skip &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;MDS was formatted with version $format_ver&quot;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I will submit a patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493048" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 13 Apr 2026 22:21:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Andreas Dilger &amp;lt;adilger@thelustrecollective.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65283&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65283&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
