                            <comment id="493054" author="JIRAUSER19404" created="Tue, 14 Apr 2026 02:31:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks, Andreas! Would it be possible for me to receive bug alerts directly in the future, so it doesn&#8217;t put extra burden on you? That said, I&apos;m not familiar with landing procedure, so I may need to consult you occasionally.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="493059" author="adilger" created="Tue, 14 Apr 2026 04:40:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;AFAIK, you can subscribe to new Jira tickets in your account settings.  However, there are a &lt;b&gt;lot&lt;/b&gt; of them and it isn&apos;t clear which ones are of interest to you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I saw this issue because of test failures related to my patch and investigated.   One place to look for common subtest failures that need to be fixed is the &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/reports?client_branch=master&amp;amp;server_branch=master&amp;amp;count=50&amp;amp;horizon=518400&amp;amp;test_type=sub+test&amp;amp;source=top_failing#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;Top Failing Tests Report&lt;/a&gt;.  Fixing intermittent test failures helps everyone&apos;s patches pass testing more consistently, so this is always useful to review.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m of course happy to help you if you have questions.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
